==============================================================================================================
L102 -- verify astra's parameter-free deep-MOND action-angle invariant; two-tracer test + Kepler split
==============================================================================================================

==============================================================================================================
PART 0 -- CONTROL: deep MOND around a point baryonic mass is a scale-free logarithmic potential.
==============================================================================================================
  [PASS] CTRL-1  the deep-MOND circular speed is v0=(G M_b a0)^{1/4}, INDEPENDENT of radius (a flat rotation curve); equivalently the potential is Phi=v0^2 ln r, whose force v0^2/r is scale-free (homogeneous degree -1). This is the structural reason a dimensionless orbit invariant exists   (v0 = 105.6 km/s (can) / 110.6 km/s (alt) for 1e10 Msun; flat (r-independent))
  [PASS] CTRL-2  the dimensionless effective potential ln rho + 1/(2 rho^2) has its circular minimum at rho=1 (value 1/2); for energy eps>1/2 there are two turning points (peri<1<apo), a bound rosette orbit   (eps=0.9: rho_peri=0.5928 < 1 < rho_apo=2.2229, e=0.579)

==============================================================================================================
PART 1 -- the dimensionless invariant I(e)=T_r v0^2/ell computed by quadrature vs eccentricity.
==============================================================================================================
